Name: Michael Bachman
Project: Movie Blender

Recommendations are made by averaging weighted vector embeddings of each movie
and finding the N closest movies (by cosine similarity) to the resulting average
vector.

Embeddings were created by training a latent-factor model with 50 factors. 
Each movie's metadata was added to the embedding vector as well, by creating a countvectorized soup
of the director (weighted 2x), writers, keywords (weighted 2x), and genres (weighted 7x). 
Lastly, the popularity and average rating of each movie are added to the vector. 

Notes:
- Used the MovieLens latest rating dataset, containing ~33,000,000 ratings. This
dataset only has info on movies up to 2023, so all recent movies are not included
in this project.
- All other movie information was gathered from TMDB

This website is the result of my 2026 summer project. Other documentation on this
project and my early experimentation with recommendation systems can be found at 
these two notebooks:

